## Lore

Northern Gun''s Bush Pilots haul cargo to remote mining sites, mercenary camps, war zones, frontier towns and logging camps: part Wilderness Scout, part Operator, part gun toting Merc Soldier, and part stunt pilot with nerves of steel. They fly ground vehicles, aircraft, boats or robots in and out of places with no runway, through bad weather and enemy fire. Combat is not what they look for; the goal is to deliver the cargo or passenger in one piece and on time, and to live to tell about it. Say "impossible" or "suicide mission" and a Bush Pilot is intrigued.

Most try to stay out of politics and may end up working for both sides of a conflict, though most avoid working for monsters, demons and true evildoers. They are famous for overflights of the Xiticix Hivelands and for supplying guerrillas during the Siege on Tolkeen, and Northern Gun sometimes uses them to deploy Loss Prevention Officers or mercenaries discreetly.

Alignment: Any, but almost always Unprincipled or Anarchist. Most of Northern Gun''s Bush Pilots are human (90+%), but there are independent pilots from many D-Bee races.

## Equipment

A Northern Gun weapon for each W.P. with four extra E-Clips for each, an NG-S2 Survival Kit, light or medium NG body armor of choice, two NG Bush Pilot Armored Jumpsuits, one mechanic''s jump suit, a flight helmet with built-in radio and nightvision goggles (may be installed in a body armor helmet), a parachute, a field computer with navigation software, 8 flares, compass, canteen and hiking boots.

NG Bush Pilot Armored Jumpsuit: resilient M.D.C. micro-fiber with extra padding in the shoulders and chest and plates in the legs; no movement penalties; camouflage colors. M.D.C. by location: helmet 35, arms 9 each, legs 20 each, main body 25. Cost: 18,000 credits.

Starts with one large truck or aircraft, often a Sky King or Skyshadow bush plane, or a float version or Kingfisher seaplane for lake work; Northern Gun lets its pilots use whatever aircraft they own or prefer. Also one Rocket Bike or hovercycle for smuggling runs, scouting and fast escapes.

## Pay and cybernetics

Pilots are paid on completion of the job. A drop into a hot zone or contraband run into a high risk zone pays 10,000-40,000 credits; moderately dangerous deliveries 3,000-12,000; simple runs 1,000-4,000.

Bush Pilots often have 2D4 minor cybernetic implants: Multi-Optic Eyes, nightvision or other optical enhancements, sometimes Cyber-Disguises and other common items.
